 binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0452768a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4eeefef9fc806102\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33597540035335144, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1400649862190735, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7930997, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0452768a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 927, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:14\", \"token_count\": 288, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Issue\\n\\nPath arguments containing backslashes (Windows-style, e.g. `C:\\\\docs\\\\input.pdf`) were mishandled by the CLI's path parser, which had only been exercised against forward-slash paths on Linux/macOS.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nPath arguments are now normalized to the platform-native separator before they reach the file-loading code, rather than assuming forward slashes everywhere.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-23\\n\\n# Windows Backslash Path Handling Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2023\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-19 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-10)\\n\\nRetrospective note on the path-handling fix made 2026-08-10 for CIPH-39 (Windows Compatibility).\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis note covers path-string handling only. It does not cover code signing or Windows Defender/SmartScreen behavior — those are separate, later concerns for CIPH-39 and are not addressed here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat issu path argument contain backslash window style e g c doc input pdf were mishandl by the cli s path parser which had onli been exercis against forward slash path on linux maco sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat fix path argument are now normal to the platform nativ separ befor they reach the file load code rather than assum forward slash everywher sourc id src gdoc 23 window backslash path handl note owner evan document key doc 2023 last updat 2026 08 19 retrospect cover 2026 08 10 retrospect note on the path handl fix made 2026 08 10 for ciph 39 window compat scope this note cover path string handl onli it doe not cover code sign or window defend smartscreen behavior those are separ later concern for ciph 39 and are not address here\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eeb39c7c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-19-Windows-Compatibility-Review.md\", \"id\": \"f22d5520af58ce07\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29877035541384966, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11672082201978527, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7235526, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-19-Windows-Compatibility-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eeb39c7c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-19-Windows-Compatibility-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-19-Windows-Compatibility-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 849, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:37\", \"token_count\": 390, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie opened on the AGPL PDF-parser problem and the search for an Apache/MIT alternative. Evan noted the earlier Windows path fix; code-signing cert procurement remains open.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-08\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Windows & License Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: Licensing first — the replacement PDF parser Evan swapped in turned out to be AGPL. I've started searching for an Apache or MIT alternative. Need to confirm feature coverage before we swap again.\\n\\n**Diana**: Right — AGPL isn't acceptable for how we're distributing the toolkit.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Unknown how much rework another swap costs until I compare candidates. That's this week's task. I'd rather not guess.\\n\\n**Evan**: Separate note while we're all here — the Windows backslash path handling fix from earlier this month has been holding up fine in the build. No regressions there.\\n\\n**Alice**: Good to hear. And signing?\\n\\n**Evan**: Still waiting on the code-signing certificate to come through procurement. No firm timeline yet, so I can't say when that's cleared.\\n\\n**Alice**: Okay — Charlie, keep pushing on the parser alternative, that's the priority. Evan, keep chasing procurement on the cert, but no need for a deep-dive there today.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli open on the agpl pdf parser problem and the search for an apach mit altern evan note the earlier window path fix code sign cert procur remain open sourc id src meet 08 firefli transcript window licens sync date 2026 08 15 particip alic pm charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli licens first the replac pdf parser evan swap in turn out to be agpl i ve start search for an apach or mit altern need to confirm featur coverag befor we swap again diana right agpl isn t accept for how we re distribut the toolkit charli unknown how much rework anoth swap cost until i compar candid that s this week s task i d rather not guess evan separ note while we re all here the window backslash path handl fix from earlier this month ha been hold up fine in the build no regress there alic good to hear and sign evan still wait on the code sign certif to come through procur no firm timelin yet so i can t say when that s clear alic okay charli keep push on the parser altern that s the prioriti evan keep chase procur on the cert but no need for a deep dive there today\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee3d8c1c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"2ef58dc2a22c77d0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28409764212084854, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10115804588692646, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7109567, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee3d8c1c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-15-Windows-License-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1335, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:20\", \"token_count\": 372, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-38\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Build Artifact\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:05] Evan**: Path fix unblocked the Windows packaging attempt — I've got a build artifact out the other end now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:06] Bob**: Does it actually run, or just build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:24] Evan**: Runs. Installed it on a Windows box and it's passing the same sanity checks we run on Linux.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:26] Diana**: Does this mean Windows compatibility is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:36] Evan**: The engineering work for the Windows build is complete — packaging works, the binary is sound. Code-signing is a separate item we haven't even started on yet, so I wouldn't call the whole thing closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:45] Alice**: Understood, we'll track signing on its own. Good progress on the build itself.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 38 slack thread window build artifact channel releas date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 05 evan path fix unblock the window packag attempt i ve got a build artifact out the other end now 2026 08 12 09 06 bob doe it actual run or just build 2026 08 12 09 24 evan run instal it on a window box and it s pass the same saniti check we run on linux 2026 08 12 09 26 diana doe this mean window compat is done 2026 08 12 09 36 evan the engin work for the window build is complet packag work the binari is sound code sign is a separ item we haven t even start on yet so i wouldn t call the whole thing close 2026 08 12 09 45 alic understood we ll track sign on it own good progress on the build itself\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edd924d48a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"id\": \"da5e0b9bbbeae005\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28209328212084855, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10115804588692646, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7042755, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edd924d48a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communicatio