own, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee3a6b908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"c466edd67f6ef08b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27074261047434794, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09337665782049706, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6845965, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee3a6b908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:22\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-11\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-11\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-11\\n\\n**Title**: Core Redaction Engine\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-01\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild the core document-redaction processing engine for CipherDoc (WS-01): the foundational component that applies redaction to detected PII regions and underlies later API, CLI, and detection work. Diana reviewed the engine and marked it Completed on 2026-06-05. On 2026-07-14 the completed engine's status was archived as evidence for the T011 release-gate checklist.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-11\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-11\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-11\\n\\n**Title**: Core Redaction Engine\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-01\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Core redaction engine implementation reviewed and approved (Diana, 2026-06-05).\\n\\n- Completed-engine record available as durable evidence for the T011 release checklist.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-11\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-11\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-11\\n\\n**Title**: Core Redaction Engine\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-01\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild the core document-redaction processing engine for CipherDoc (WS-01): the foundational component that applies redaction to detected PII regions and underlies later API, CLI, and detection work. Diana reviewed the engine and marked it Completed on 2026-06-05. On 2026-07-14 the completed engine's status was archived as evidence for the T011 release-gate checklist.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-11\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-11\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-11\\n\\n**Title**: Core Redaction Engine\\n\\n**Status**: Completed\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-01\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-06-01**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Task opened to build the core redaction engine.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 11 sourc id src cu ciph 11 task id ciph 11 titl core redact engin status complet assigne charli prioriti high date creat 2026 06 01 descript build the core document redact process engin for cipherdoc w 01 the foundat compon that appli redact to detect pii region and under later api cli and detect work diana review the engin and mark it complet on 2026 06 05 on 2026 07 14 the complet engin s status wa archiv a evid for the t011 releas gate checklist clickup task ciph 11 sourc id src cu ciph 11 task id ciph 11 titl core redact engin status complet assigne charli prioriti high date creat 2026 06 01 accept criterion core redact engin implement review and approv diana 2026 06 05 complet engin record avail a durabl evid for the t011 releas checklist clickup task ciph 11 sourc id src cu ciph 11 task id ciph 11 titl core redact engin status complet assigne charli prioriti high date creat 2026 06 01 descript build the core document redact process engin for cipherdoc w 01 the foundat compon that appli redact to detect pii region and under later api cli and detect work diana review the engin and mark it complet on 2026 06 05 on 2026 07 14 the complet engin s status wa archiv a evid for the t011 releas gate checklist clickup task ciph 11 sourc id src cu ciph 11 task id ciph 11 titl core redact engin status complet assigne charli prioriti high date creat 2026 06 01 activ histori 2026 06 01 alic task creat open task open to build the core redact engin\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee40ead88a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-11-Core-Redaction-Engine.md\", \"id\": \"0158140a70ac7384\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26200946882784737, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08559526975406766, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6736426, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-11-Core-Redaction-Engine.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee40ead88a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-11-Core-Redaction-Engine.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-11-Core-Redaction-Engine.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1218, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:17\", \"token_count\": 599, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 10 11 51 charli flatten might work but it ll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layer 2026 09 10 12 29 alic diana charli let s leav high dpi render block for now we need to decid if we can ship with this limit or if we need a differ render librari entir 2026 09 10 12 32 diana agre it onli aff