 coordinates the rendering library reports for the same region.\\n\\n3. At scale factors above 1.0, the overlay box is offset from the actual text region, with the offset growing as scale factor increases.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nThe misalignment reproduces consistently at both tested scale factors. It does not reproduce at 100% scale.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-30\\n\\n# Document: High-DPI-Coordinate-Misalignment-Repro\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2030\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-17)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nRoot cause has not been isolated as part of this reproduction pass; this note only establishes that the defect reproduces and under which display conditions.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 test log reproduct note for the high dpi coordin misalign report for ciph 46 first reproduc 2026 08 17 sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 repro step 1 open a pdf on a display report a scale factor abov 10 test at 150 and 200 2 compar the redact preview overlay s report box coordin against the coordin the render librari report for the same region 3 at scale factor abov 10 the overlay box is offset from the actual text region with the offset grow a scale factor increas sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 result the misalign reproduc consist at both test scale factor it doe not reproduc at 100 scale sourc id src gdoc 30 document high dpi coordin misalign repro owner charli document key doc 2030 last updat 2026 09 02 retrospect cover 2026 08 17 status root caus ha not been isol a part of this reproduct pas this note onli establish that the defect reproduc and under which display condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee87b8968a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"id\": \"99b368dd772283f8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37718384134070904, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18410951620101285, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8276906, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee87b8968a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Fixes-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 987, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:14\", \"token_count\": 453, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 10 11 51 charli flatten might work but it ll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layer 2026 09 10 12 29 alic diana charli let s leav high dpi render block for now we need to decid if we can ship with this limit or if we need a differ render librari entir 2026 09 10 12 32 diana agre it onli affect a small subset of complex document but we should document it a a known issu\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee20a43a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"id\": \"66a2899f0f7ec51f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37405761346921895, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18392977352745574, \"vector_similarity\": 0.81768924, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee20a43a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1371, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:47\", \"token_count\": 414, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-49\\n\\n# Technical Report: High-DPI Coordinate Scaling — Upstream Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2049\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n## Background\\n\\nEarlier work (2026-08-17) reproduced misalignment on 4K displays. Follow-on scaling math (2026-08-19) was checked against the Completed preview-overlay coordinates from T023.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-49\\n\\n# Technical Report: High-DPI Coordinate Scaling — Upstream Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2049\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n## Finding\\n\\nThe scaling error points to a defect in the upstream rendering library's scaling math. No safe local fix has been identified yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-49\\n\\n# Technical Report: High-DPI Coordinate Scaling — Upstream Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2049\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n## Current Status: Blocked\\n\\nT036 is Blocked on that upstream library issue. Local coordinate work remains dependent on T023's overlay path but cannot clear the gate until upstream scaling is corrected or an accepted local remediation is chosen.\\n\\n*Status*: Blocked on upstream rendering-library scaling math.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 49 technic report high dpi coordin scale upstream block owner diana document key doc 2049 last updat 2026 09 10 background earlier work 2026 08 17 reproduc misalign on 4k display follow on scale math 2026 08 19 wa check against the complet preview overlay coordin from t023 sourc id src gdoc 49 technic report high dpi coordin scale upstream block owner diana document key doc 2049 last updat 2026 09 10 find the scale error point to a defect in the upstream render librari s scale math no safe local fix ha been identifi yet sourc id src gdoc 49 technic report high dpi coordin scale upstream block owner diana document key doc 2049 last updat 2026 09 10 current status block t036 is block on that upstream librari issu local coordin work remain depend on t023 s overlay path but can not clear the gate until upstream scale is correct or an accept local remedi is chosen status block on upstream render librari scale math\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"eeaf73188a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-10-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Coordinates-Report.md\", \"id\": \"88dd78dc4ecdb2a5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3461364059924871, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14065217998926724, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8255996, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-10-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Coordinates-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"eeaf73188a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-10-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Coordinates-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-10-High-DPI-PDF-Rendering-Coordinates-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 808, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:40\", \"token_count\": 306, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-57\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Scaling Math\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-19\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-19 13:51] Charlie**: Okay, I've updated the scaling math to use the `pdf-renderer`'s internal viewport dimensions instead of raw screen pixels, and cross-checked it against the preview-overlay coordinates from the redaction preview work — that's where the scale-factor error was showing up most.\\n\\n**[2026-08-19 14:26] Diana**: I'm still seeing a 1-2 pixel drift on some documents. It's better, but not perfect.\\n\\n**[2026-08-19 14:31] Charlie**: Are those documents rotated? I might need to check the rotation matrix too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-19 14:34] Diana**: Yeah, the one that's drifting is a landscape scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-19 14:39] Charlie**: Got it. The coordinate transform for rotated pages in PDF is notorious. I'll add a check for the `/Rotate` key in the page dictionary.\\n\\n**[2026-08-19 14:41] Bob**: @Charlie do we need to worry about different DPIs between monitors in a multi-head setup?\\n\\n**[2026-08-19 14:44] Charlie**: Hopefully not if we stay in PDF point-space. I'll verify that tomorrow.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 57 slack thread high dpi scale math channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 19 2026 08 19 13 51 charli okay i ve updat the scale math to use the pdf render s intern viewport dimens instead of raw screen pixel and cross check it against the preview overlay coordin from the redact preview work that s where the scale factor error wa show up most 2026 08 19 14 26 diana i m still see a1 2 pixel drift on some document it s better but not perfect 2026 08 19 14 31 charli are those document rotat i might need to check the rotat matrix too 2026 08 19 14 34 diana yeah the one that s drift is a landscap scan 2026 08 19 14 39 charli got it the coordin transform for rotat page in pdf is notori i ll add a check for the rotat key in the page dictionari 2026 08 19 14 41 bob charli do we need to worri about differ dpis between monitor in a multi head setup 2026 08 19 14 44 charli hope not if we stay in pdf point space i ll verifi that tomorrow\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edfc699e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-19-high-dpi-scaling-math.md\", \"id\": \"30bbb730e62b82d2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28938492164657215, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08655518806653166, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7626543, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-19-high-dpi-scaling-math.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edfc699e8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-19-high-dpi-scaling-math.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-19-high-dpi-scaling-math.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1125, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:21\", \"token_count\": 338, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-56\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Repro\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-17\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:13] Charlie**: Finally reproduced the offset mismatch on 4K displays. It looks like we're not accounting for the device pixel ratio when calculating the bounding box for the redaction masks.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:15] Diana**: That explains why my screenshots were always slightly off to the left on the high-res monitor.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:18] Charlie**: Exactly. The internal coordinate system is in PDF points (72 DPI), but the renderer is using pixels. On a 4K screen with 200% scaling, that offset is doubled.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:21] Bob**: Are we doing the math in the engine or the preview UI?\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:30] Charlie**: It's happening in the `BoundingBoxTranslator` in the engine. I need to normalize everything back to the raw PDF dimensions before we generate the mask.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 10:32] Alice**: @Charlie how long for a fix? This is blocking the final verification of the preview UI for high-res users.\\n\\n**[2026-08-17 11:00] Charlie**: I'm working on the scaling math now. Should have a PR for testing by tomorrow.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 56 slack thread high dpi repro channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 17 2026 08 17 10 13 charli final reproduc the offset mismatch on 4k display it look like we re not account for the devic pixel ratio when calcul the bound box for the redact mask 2026 08 17 1015 diana that explain whi my screenshot were alway slight off to the left on the high re monitor 2026 08 17 1018 charli exact the intern coordin system is in pdf point 72 dpi but the render is use pixel on a 4k screen with 200 scale that offset is doubl 2026 08 17 10 21 bob are we do the math in the engin or the preview ui 2026 08 17 10 30 charli it s happen in the boundingboxtransl in the engin i need to normal everyth back to the raw pdf dimens befor we generat the mask 2026 08 17 10 32 alic charli how long for a fix this is block the final verif of the preview ui for high re user 2026 08 17 11 00 charli i m work on the scale math now should have a pr for test by tomorrow\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee0e675c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-high-dpi-repro.md\", \"id\": \"632b4e7cae20bc5f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28107358234279767, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07032609048971099, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77281773, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-high-dpi-repro.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee0e675c8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-high-dpi-repro.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-17-high-dpi-repro.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1156, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:04\", \"token_count\": 340, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee3a6b908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"c466edd67f6ef08b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27756620995034664, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10278428564335235, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6853907, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee3a6b908a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:22\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-05\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offset Mismatch Debugging\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-23\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 08:56] Charlie**: @Diana, I'm seeing weird behavior in the test cases. The redaction masks are shifted by a character or two in some PDF exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 09:01] Diana**: Multi-column layouts? I told you pdfminer output was injecting spaces.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 09:43] Charlie**: It's not just the spaces. The engine sees the text at one offset, but the PDF coordinates are different after the cleaning phase.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:51] Diana**: Are you seeing this on all viewers? Sometimes Acrobat renders overlays differently than Chrome's PDF viewer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:52] Charlie**: Looking at the raw coordinate output for now. Whitespace normalization looks like the culprit — non-breaking spaces keep showing up in the extracted text.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 10:53] Charlie**: Still stuck. Tried mapping cleaned offsets back to raw ones, but the math falls apart on dense pages.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:40] Diana**: Can we get most of the standard text aligned and park the edge cases?\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:42] Charlie**: Not really — on dense docs it's closer to half the spans. Starting to look like an upstream pdfminer.six issue. I'm going to check their tracker.\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:45] Alice**: Status?\\n\\n**[2026-06-23 12:47] Charlie**: No. Offline tonight.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 05 slack thread offset mismatch debug channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 23 2026 06 23 08 56 charli diana i m see weird behavior in the test case the redact mask are shift by a charact or two in some pdf export 2026 06 23 09 01 diana multi column layout i told you pdfminer output wa inject space 2026 06 23 09 43 charli it s not just the space the engin see the text at one offset but the pdf coordin are differ after the clean phase 2026 06 23 10 51 diana are you see this on all viewer sometim acrobat render overlay differ than chrome s pdf viewer 2026 06 23 10 52 charli look at the raw coordin output for now whitespac normal look like the culprit non break space keep show up in the extract text 2026 06 23 10 53 charli still stuck tri map clean offset back to raw one but the math fall apart on dens page 2026 06 23 12 40 diana can we get most of the standard text align and park the edg case 2026 06 23 12 42 charli not realli on dens doc it s closer to half the span start to look like an upstream pdfminer six issu i m go to check their tracker 2026 06 23 12 45 alic status 2026 06 23 12 47 charli no offlin tonight\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee2707448a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"id\": \"30c128c9ab691c29\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2732748907773892, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07573578968198455, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73419946, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee2707448a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-23-offset-bug-debug.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1387, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:41\", \"token_count\": 405, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Title**: Fix Coordinate/Offset Drift in Multi-Page PDFs\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-19\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-06-19**: Bob - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Task opened to investigate the coordinate/offset drift in multi-page PDF redaction.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"titl fix coordin offset drift in multi page pdfs status block assigne charli prioriti high date creat 2026 06 19 activ histori 2026 06