 cli integr activ wire audit log generat into the cli path now that the schema wa defin to satisfi the releas gate 2026 09 18 diana audit verifi mismatch activ verif found the cli emit audit record inconsist with the defin schema this mismatch remain an open releas blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee5c42ce8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"id\": \"27857d38103c6293\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2976832778669662, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12240752695280888, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70666003, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee5c42ce8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2011, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:52\", \"token_count\": 759, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"CIPH-29 offline authentication key escrow T019 release gate v1.0 release blocker\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37"],"question":"CMT-2026-08-001 release gate ship v1 key escrow offline CipherDoc","metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37"],"question":"CMT-2026-08-001 release gate ship v1 key escrow offline CipherDoc","metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Sign-off Basis\\n\\nSecurity sign-off on the AES-256 at-rest pipeline was withheld until the fail-closed deletion behavior for interrupted redaction runs (T015) was confirmed Completed — an unencrypted partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermined the encryption guarantee entirely. With that dependency cleared, the sign-off proceeded against the pipeline as implemented.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## What Was Reviewed\\n\\n- AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption applied to every redacted output file before it is written to its final location.\\n\\n- Key handling confined to process memory; no plaintext key material written to disk or logs.\\n\\n- Confirmed the pipeline degrades safely (refuses to write plaintext) if key material is unavailable, consistent with the fail-closed contract from T015.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-35\\n\\n# Crypto Sign-off: AES-256 At-Rest Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2035\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n## Follow-up Noted at Sign-off\\n\\nOn machines without a hardware TPM, the volume key is still derived from a user passphrase via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 100k iterations. This is not a blocker for the AES-256 pipeline sign-off itself, but Diana flagged it as a hardening follow-up: moving to Argon2id would meaningfully raise the cost of offline brute-force against weak passphrases on non-TPM hardware.\\n\\n*Status*: AES-256 at-rest pipeline signed off as Completed. Passphrase-derived key hardening (Argon2id) tracked separately as a pre-v1.0 hardening item, not a sign-off condition.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 sign off basi secur sign off on the ae 256 at rest pipelin wa withheld until the fail close delet behavior for interrupt redact run t015 wa confirm complet an unencrypt partial output left on disk after a crash would have undermin the encrypt guarante entir with that depend clear the sign off proceed against the pipelin a implement sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 what wa review ae 256 gcm authent encrypt appli to everi redact output file befor it is written to it final locat key handl confin to process memori no plaintext key materi written to disk or log confirm the pipelin degrad safe refus to write plaintext if key materi is unavail consist with the fail close contract from t015 sourc id src gdoc 35 crypto sign off ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin owner diana document key doc 2035 last updat 2026 08 07 follow up note at sign off on machin without a hardwar tpm the volum key is still deriv from a user passphras via pbkdf2 hmac sha256 at 100k iter this is not a blocker for the ae 256 pipelin sign off itself but diana flag it a a harden follow up move to argon2id would meaning rais the cost of offlin brute forc against weak passphras on non tpm hardwar status ae 256 at rest pipelin sign off a complet passphras deriv key harden argon2id track separ a a pre v1 0 harden item not a sign off condit\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee8945628a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"id\": \"b911da0ec59b38de\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37347930667578194, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20148806667968852, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7747922, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee8945628a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-07-Local-Encryption-at-Rest-Security-Evaluation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1518, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:12\", \"token_count\": 466, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-16\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Mode Authentication Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 11:14] Diana**: Starting on offline-mode auth design. If we're running air-gapped, we can't call home for license validation or user auth, so key rotation can't assume an always-on network either.\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 11:16] Alice**: Right — whatever we design has to keep working with no connection for extended stretches.\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 11:22] Diana**: I'm sketching a rotation flow built around a locally held key rather than one that needs a live call to rotate.\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 13:00] Alice**: How do we actually rotate it if the site is air-gapped?\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 14:24] Diana**: Still working that part out — that's the piece I'm least confident about. I'll have a first draft of the design by Wednesday.\\n\\n**[2026-08-02 14:27] Diana**: I'll loop in Bob once the draft's ready so he can start mocking it for testing.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 16 slack thread offlin mode authent design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 02 2026 08 02 11 14 diana start on offlin mode auth design if we re run air gap we can t call home for licens valid or user auth so key rotat can t assum an alway on network either 2026 08 02 11 16 alic right whatev we design ha to keep work with no connect for extend stretch 2026 08 02 11 22 diana i m sketch a rotat flow built around a local held key rather than one that need a live call to rotat 2026 08 02 13 00 alic how do we actual rotat it if the site is air gap 2026 08 02 14 24 diana still work that part out that s the piec i m least confid about i ll have a first draft of the design by wednesday 2026 08 02 14 27 diana i ll loop in bob onc the draft s readi so he can start mock it for test\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee02ac008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-02-offline-auth-key-rotation.md\", \"id\": \"585e209a330d2aa1\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.364793967436453, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19658521348064717, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75728106, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-02-offline-auth-key-rotation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee02ac008a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-02-offline-auth-key-rotation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-02-offline-auth-key-rotation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 965, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:08:15\", \"token_count\": 291, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-20\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Local Encryption at Rest — Crypto Evaluation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-03\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:02] Bob**: Starting on local encryption at rest. Redacted outputs that hit disk need to be encrypted, and it has to work with no network dependency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:30] Charlie**: Any library lean yet?\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 11:48] Bob**: Evaluating options for AES-256 that fit the offline runtime. Want something we can ship without cloud KMS.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 13:45] Diana**: Application-level on the outputs, or wrapping the whole volume?\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 13:54] Bob**: Application-level on the redacted outputs. More portable across the workstations we're targeting.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 14:03] Alice**: Keep the eval focused on AES-256 at rest for local outputs. Implementation can follow once you've picked a library path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-03 14:40] Bob**: Will do. Next step after this is wiring the pipeline once the library choice is settled.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 20 slack thread local encrypt at rest crypto evalu channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 03 2026 08 03 11 02 bob start on local encrypt at rest redact output that hit disk need to be encrypt and it ha to work with no network depend 2026 08 03 11 30 charli ani librari lean yet 2026 08 03 11 48 bob evalu option for ae 256 that fit the offlin runtim want someth we can ship without cloud km 2026 08 03 13 45 diana applic level on the output or wrap the whole volum 2026 08 03 13 54 bob applic level on the redact output more portabl across the workstat we re target 2026 08 03 14 03 alic keep the eval focus on ae 256 at rest for local output implement can follow onc you ve pick a librari path 2026 08 03 14 40 bob will do next step after this is wire the pipelin onc the librari choic is settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edc587768a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-aes256-crypto-eval.md\", \"id\": \"0d8a3376fd7823f3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.364122414436453, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19658521348064717, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75504255, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-aes256-crypto-eval.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edc587768a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-aes256-crypto-eval.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-03-aes256-crypto-eval.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 992, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:11\", \"token_count\": 299, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMake the redaction suite compatible with Windows, including build packaging. A Windows build artifact now exists, but Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; the task remains active pending that certificate.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Windows build artifact is produced successfully.\\n\\n- Build is code-signed with a valid certificate so it is not blocked by Defender/SmartScreen.\\n\\n- Signed build passes Windows Defender/SmartScreen without warnings.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMake the redaction suite compatible with Windows, including build packaging. A Windows build artifact now exists, but Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; the task remains active pending that certificate.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-39\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-39\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Windows builds and clear Defender/SmartScreen signing\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-08**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because Windows OS compatibility is required for the release gate.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-02**: Evan - Signing Cert Missing (Active)\\n\\n - *Found that Windows Defender/SmartScreen blocks the unsigned build because a code-signing certificate is still missing; task remains active.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 descript make the redact suit compat with window includ build packag a window build artifact now exist but window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss the task remain activ pend that certif clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 accept criterion window build artifact is produc success build is code sign with a valid certif so it is not block by defend smartscreen sign build pass window defend smartscreen without warn clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 descript make the redact suit compat with window includ build packag a window build artifact now exist but window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss the task remain activ pend that certif clickup task ciph 39 sourc id src cu ciph 39 task id ciph 39 titl fix window build and clear defend smartscreen sign status activ assigne evan prioriti high date creat 2026 08 08 activ histori 2026 08 08 alic task creat open open the task becaus window o compat is requir for the releas gate 2026 09 02 evan sign cert miss activ found that window defend smartscreen block the unsign build becaus a code sign certif is still miss task remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee4d7cc68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"id\": \"9cf930da8c6d2e36\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3589631894241906, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20469298489170082, \"vector_similarity\": 0.718927, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee4d7cc68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-39-Windows-Compatibility.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1115, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:07:07\", \"token_count\": 532, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-17\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Offline Auth Mock and Rotation Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:14] Bob**: Building the local auth mock for air-gap testing so we can exercise Diana's key-rotation design without a real deployment.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 09:16] Bob**: Mock is up. It runs the rotation flow with the network disabled, same as a real air-gapped site would see.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 10:27] Diana**: Good, that's exactly what I need to validate the design against.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:36] Alice**: How'd it go?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:45] Bob**: Not great. Key rotation just can't complete with the network down — the flow we designed assumes at least a brief connection to finish the handshake.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 08:48] Alice**: Ugh.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:13] Diana**: So we're blocked. There's no resolution yet on how to rotate without any network at all.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:33] Alice**: Offline auth stays blocked. Let's regroup on whether the design needs to change or whether we relax the offline requirement.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 17 slack thread offlin auth mock and rotat block channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 04 last activ 2026 08 05 2026 08 04 09 14 bob build the local auth mock for air gap test so we can exercis diana s key rotat design without a real deploy 2026 08 04 09 16 bob mock is up it run the rotat flow with the network disabl same a a real air gap site would see 2026 08 04 10 27 diana good that s exact what i need to valid the design against 2026 08 05 08 36 alic how d it go 2026 08 05 08 45 bob not great key rotat just can t complet with the network down the flow we design assum at least a brief connect to finish the handshak 2026 08 05 08 48 alic ugh 2026 08 05 09 13 diana so we re block there s no resolut yet on how to rotat without ani network at all 2026 08 05 09 33 alic offlin auth stay block let s regroup on whether the design need to chang or whether we relax the offlin requir\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edbb698a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"id\": \"28867d857abb09be\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.354151644436453, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19658521348064717, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72180665, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"edbb698a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-offline-auth-mock-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1092, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:14\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:18\", \"token_count\": 340, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-13\\n\\n# Offline-Mode Authentication — Key-Rotation Design\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2013\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n**Constraint**: T019 must support authentication for air-gapped deployments where an always-on network cannot be assumed.\\n\\n## Design Focus\\n\\nWorking out a key-rotation flow that does not depend on continuous network reachability, since the target deployments are air-gapped.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-13\\n\\n# Offline-Mode Authentication — Key-Rotation Design\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2013\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n**Constraint**: T019 must support authentication for air-gapped deployments where an always-on network cannot be assumed.\\n\\n## Open Question\\n\\nHow rotation behaves for a workstation that stays offline for an extended period has not been validated yet — that check is expected once a local auth mock exists.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-13\\n\\n# Offline-Mode Authentication — Key-Rotation Design\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2013\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-02\\n\\n**Constraint**: T019 must support authentication for air-gapped deployments where an always-on network cannot be assumed.\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nActive — design stage.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 13 offlin mode authent key rotat design owner diana document key doc 2013 last updat 2026 08 02 constraint t019 must support authent for air gap deploy where an alway on network can not be assum design focus work out a key rotat flow that doe not depend on continu network reachabl sinc the target deploy are air gap sourc id src gdoc 13 offlin mode authent key rotat design owner diana document key doc 2013 last updat 2026 08 02 constraint t019 must support authent for air gap deploy where an alway on network can not be assum open question how rotat behav for a workstat that stay offlin for an extend period ha not been valid yet that check is expect onc a local auth mock exist sourc id src gdoc 13 offlin mode authent key rotat design owner diana document key doc 2013 last updat 2026 08 02 constraint t019 must support authent for air gap deploy where an alway on network can not be assum status activ design stage\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee8cbbb68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-02-Offline-Mode-Authentication-Review.md\", \"id\": \"7ee3a796e9e8f933\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.353996839460978, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18036967065853995, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7591269, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-02-Offline-Mode-Authentication-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee8cbbb68a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-02-Offline-Mode-Authentication-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-02-Offline-Mode-Authentication-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 650, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:06\", \"token_count\": 300, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## What Was Run\\n\\nA full batch redaction run was executed under the offline test harness (T027) with network access denied, using a local sample document set. The run depended on the completed AES-256 at-rest encryption pipeline (T021), since offline output still needs to be encrypted without any network-based key service.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nThe batch completed successfully end-to-end with the network denied: no network-dependent call blocked the run, and local policy parsing worked entirely from bundled definitions.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Noted Issue: 45-Second Licence-Check Hang\\n\\nThe run was not clean — the HTTP client attempted to verify the license key against a remote server before timing out and falling back to the cached local license, adding roughly 45 seconds of startup delay. This is logged as a known issue, not something this sign-off waives.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Scope of This Sign-off\\n\\nThis sign-off is **preliminary** and covers functional completion of a batch run offline only. It is explicitly **not** a compliance certification — it does not cover side-channel analysis, physical security, or any regulatory attestation. No patient records or clinical data were used in this test run.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 what wa run a full batch redact run wa execut under the offlin test har t027 with network access deni use a local sampl document set the run depend on the complet ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin t021 sinc offlin output still need to be encrypt without ani network base key servic sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 result the batch complet success end to end with the network deni no network depend call block the run and local polici pars work entir from bundl definit sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 note issu 45 second licenc check hang the run wa not clean the http client attempt to verifi the licens key against a remot server befor time out and fall back to the cach local licens ad rough 45 second of startup delay this is log a a known issu not someth this sign off waif sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 scope of this sign off this sign off is preliminari and cover function complet of a batch run offlin onli it is explicit not a complianc certif it doe not cover side channel analysi physic secur or ani regulatori attest no patient record or clinic data were use in this test run\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee9b9e6a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"id\": \"3766c87791acc1a0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.353468014460978, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18036967065853995, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75736415, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee9b9e6a8a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1322, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:05:55\", \"token_count\": 456, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-21\\n\\n# Slack Thread: AES-256 Encryption Pipeline\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-07\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:20] Bob**: Moving forward with the AES-256 pipeline now that the crypto eval settled on it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:28] Bob**: Merged it — every temp file in the processing queue is now encrypted with a per-session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:37] Diana**: Running a stress test. What happens if the system loses power mid-redaction? Does the encrypted temp file persist?\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:38] Bob**: Yes, but it's useless without the session key, which only lives in volatile memory. On reboot, the cleanup hook wipes it anyway.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 09:39] Diana**: Makes sense.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:23] Diana**: Crypto sign-off done. Verified the `/tmp/cipherdoc` data is unreadable without the session key.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:41] Diana**: This also builds on the fail-closed work — the pipeline integrates with that deletion behavior cleanly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:43] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 13:44] Alice**: Nice. :white_check_mark:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 21 slack thread ae 256 encrypt pipelin channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 05 last activ 2026 08 07 2026 08 05 09 20 bob move forward with the ae 256 pipelin now that the crypto eval settl on it 2026 08 05 09 28 bob merg it everi temp file in the process queue is now encrypt with a per session key 2026 08 05 09 37 diana run a stress test what happen if the system lose power mid redact doe the encrypt temp file persist 2026 08 05 09 38 bob yes but it s useless without the session key which onli life in volatil memori on reboot the cleanup hook wipe it anyway 2026 08 05 09 39 diana make sens 2026 08 07 13 23 diana crypto sign off done verifi the tmp cipherdoc data is unread without the session key 2026 08 07 13 41 diana this also build on the fail close work the pipelin integr with that delet behavior clean 2026 08 07 13 43 bob call this done 2026 08 07 13 44 alic nice white _ check _ mark\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"docu